            <div type="translation" source="bib:Ramachandran1954_01">
                
                <p n="1">The Nāyakar God <supplied reason="explanation">Lord Buddha</supplied> of (or dedicated to) the Cōḻaperumpaḷḷi.</p>			                
            </div>
            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
                
                <p n="1">The Lord <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>nāyakar</foreign></supplied> <supplied reason="subaudible">of</supplied> the Cōḻa Perumpaḷḷi.<note>See the Smaller Leiden Plates (EI 22.35).<!--update--></note></p>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="commentary">
                <p><bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1954_01"/></bibl> comments thus: <quote>Obviously this votive image was meant for the Cōḻaperumpaḷḷi which was a celegrated Buddhist <foreign>vihāra</foreign> erected in Nāgapaṭṭiṇam by the Śailendra ruler of Śrīvijaya (in Sumatra) and named after the reigning Cōḻa king, Kulottuṅga I.</quote></p>
            </div>
            
